 #edb/ref 17592186048233 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048999 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048377 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048999 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048418 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048999 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048451 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048999 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049202 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048999 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049255 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048999 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049602 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048999 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050879 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048999 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186198355 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048999 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186198356 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048999 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186198473 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048999 #edb/ref 1031 "Differentiating Vector-Valued Functions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048999 #edb/ref 1033 4139 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048999 #edb/ref 1034 1.171346431943319 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186048999 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "d21fb3a0-a806-5c0d-82f7-6eced020fb4f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049196 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048648 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049196 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186119748 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049196 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186119749 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049196 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186119750 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049196 #edb/ref 1031 "Introduction to Curvature" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049196 #edb/ref 1033 1833 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049196 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "e289a183-5534-5388-8ee7-3fc0d8f4ee68" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049317 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048440 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049317 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049317 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048988 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049317 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049362 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049317 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049873 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049317 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050223 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049317 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050370 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049317 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050867 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049317 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186184340 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049317 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186184341 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049317 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186184342 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049317 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186184343 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049317 #edb/ref 1031 "Describing Function Composition" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049317 #edb/ref 1033 3817 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186049317 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "ebb1ef31-5cab-5892-affd-92e347cc4f35" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051045 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049196 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051045 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186119745 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051045 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186119746 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051045 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186119747 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051045 #edb/ref 1029 #edb/ref 17592186428385 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186051045 #edb/ref 1031 "Parameterization by Arc Length" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051045 #edb/ref 1033 1838 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051045 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "7cf45c34-fae0-53a3-89c2-bd091d1c7405" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117861 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186443490 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117861 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186443502 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117861 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186443513 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117861 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186443515 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117861 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186443524 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117861 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117861 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117861 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186443524 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186117861 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a151873b-5e83-57f7-8ab2-495a187820b3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119561 #edb/ref 1069 "e-3065" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119561 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the curve  $\\mathbf r(t)=\\left\\langle 2t-1 ,\\: 8t+2 ,\\: -2t \\right\\rangle, \\, t \\geq 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $\\mathbf{r}(0)$ to $\\mathbf{r}(t)$ is given by $s=6\\sqrt{2}t.$ Find $\\mathbf R(s),$ the parametrization of the curve by its arc length $s.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119561 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9b2026e3-781b-5e73-8dc2-0e8f2789fe67" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119561 #edb/ref 1074 "First, since  $s=6\\sqrt{2}t,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6\\sqrt{2}t & =s \\\\ t & =\\frac{s}{6\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ t & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vector function that pametrizes the curve $\\mathbf r(t)$ by its arc length $s,$ with $s \\geq 0,$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{12}) \\\\  & =⟨2(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{12})-1,\\,8(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{12})+2,\\,-2(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{12})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{6}-1,\\,\\frac{4\\sqrt{2}s}{6}+2,\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{6}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}⟨\\sqrt{2}s-6,\\,4\\sqrt{2}s+12,\\,-\\sqrt{2}s⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119562 #edb/ref 1069 "e-3066" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119562 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the parametrization of the curve  $\\mathbf r(t)=2(t\\cos{t}-\\sin{t})\\,\\mathbf i+2(t\\sin{t}+\\cos{t})\\,\\mathbf j, \\, t \\geq 0$ by its arc length $s?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119562 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "74f33486-6391-5ec0-8a5b-bb51c9af2d55" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119562 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find $\\mathbf{r}'(t)$ and its magnitude $\\|\\mathbf{r}'(t)\\|\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+2(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =-2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =|2t|\\sqrt{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that in the last step, we removed the absolute value bars since $t>0.$ \n\nNext, we calculate the arc length of the curve from $0$ to $t\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}‖{r}^{′}(u)‖\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}2u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={u}^{2}{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & ={t}^{2}-0 \\\\  & ={t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $s=t^2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =s \\\\ t & =\\pm \\sqrt{s} \\\\ t & =\\sqrt{s},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ntaking the positive root because $t>0.$  \n\nFinally, the vector function that parametrizes $\\mathbf r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\sqrt{s}) \\\\  & =2(\\sqrt{s}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{s}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{s})\\,i+2(\\sqrt{s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{s}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{s})\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119563 #edb/ref 1069 "e-3067" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119563 #edb/ref 1071 "Given the curve  $\\mathbf r(t)=\\cos{t}\\,\\mathbf i - \\sin{t}\\,\\mathbf j+\\sqrt{3}t\\,\\mathbf k, \\, t \\geq 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $\\mathbf r(0)$ to $\\mathbf r(t)$ is given by $s=2t,$ find the corresponding unit tangent $\\mathbf{T}(s),$ parametrized by $s.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119563 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "48350682-3ad0-5311-bb47-782ec454390c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119563 #edb/ref 1074 "First, since $s=2t,$ we have that $t=\\dfrac{s}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the vector function $\\mathbf R(s)$ that parametrizes $\\mathbf r(t)$ by its arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,j+\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\frac{s}{2}k \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}s}{2}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, since the curve is parametrized by its arc length $s,$ the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf T(s) = \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}s}\\mathbf R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}))\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}))j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}s}{2})k \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,i-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,i-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,j+\\sqrt{3}\\,k).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119745 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049317 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119745 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186120279 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119745 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186120286 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119745 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186262811 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119745 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186314853 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119745 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186319302 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119745 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186387824 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119745 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186443543 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119745 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186443544 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119745 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186443548 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186119745 #edb/ref 1039 "Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length Given Its Arc L